From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shipwright <shipwright@invalid>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:40:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Share one system bus connection and scan only while a client
 is connected

Every BlueZ proxy (one per device BlueZ knows, the adapter, the root)
was created with sdbus::createProxy(destination, path), which gives it
a system bus connection and an event loop thread of its own. With BLE
discovery running, every device in range became a BlueZ object and so
another connection: on a phone in a busy place the daemon reached the
system bus's per-user limit (256), and the user's other programs could
no longer use the system bus. All of them now share one connection
with one event loop thread (SystemBus()).

BLE discovery, for the case-open animation, ran from the session's
start for as long as it lasted, whether or not anything showed the
animation: the phone's Bluetooth settings showed it searching and the
radio never rested. It now runs only while a WebSocket client (the app)
is connected and the animation setting is on, and stops when the last
client leaves.
